NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Most providers expose native tools beyond user-defined function calls: web\nsearch, code execution, computer use, hosted retrieval, and more. TanStack AI\nexports each provider's native tools from a dedicated "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/tools"},{"type":"text","value":" subpath per\nadapter package."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You have an adapter already wired up. You want to give the model access to a\nprovider-native capability (e.g. Anthropic web search) and be sure you never\npair a tool with a model that doesn't support it. By the end of this page,\nyou'll have imported the factory, added it to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat({ tools: [...] })"},{"type":"text","value":", and\nunderstood the compile-time guard that will catch unsupported combinations."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"import","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Import"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every adapter ships provider tools on a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/tools"},{"type":"text","value":" subpath:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { webSearchTool } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic/tools'\nimport { codeInterpreterTool } from '@tanstack/ai-openai/tools'\nimport { googleSearchTool } from '@tanstack/ai-gemini/tools'","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"use-in-chat-tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat({ tools })"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { anthropicText } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\nimport { webSearchTool } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic/tools'\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: anthropicText('claude-opus-4-6'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: \"Summarize today's AI news.\" }],\n  tools: [\n    webSearchTool({\n      name: 'web_search',\n      type: 'web_search_20250305',\n      max_uses: 3,\n    }),\n  ],\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The factory is what selects native provider behavior, not the public name. A plain function named "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"web_search"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"google_search"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"code_execution"},{"type":"text","value":" stays a custom function. Do not hand-build "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ name: 'web_search', metadata: ... }"},{"type":"text","value":" and expect a native payload."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can put a factory tool and your own function in the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat({ tools })"},{"type":"text","value":" call if the names differ. Tool names in one "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tools"},{"type":"text","value":" array must be unique. If you pass both "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"webSearchTool()"},{"type":"text","value":" and your own function named "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"web_search"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" throws "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DuplicateToolNameError"},{"type":"text","value":" before it talks to the provider."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"multi-turn-persistence","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Multi-turn persistence"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider tools run on the provider's own infrastructure, so their results\n(e.g. Anthropic "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"web_search"},{"type":"text","value":" sources, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"web_fetch"},{"type":"text","value":" page contents) come back\nembedded in the assistant turn rather than as a separate tool message. TanStack\nAI preserves those results on the assistant message, so when you feed the prior\nconversation back into the next "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" call the model still sees the earlier\nevidence — no special handling required:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, StreamProcessor } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { anthropicText } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\nimport { webSearchTool } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic/tools'\n\nconst adapter = anthropicText('claude-opus-4-6')\nconst tools = [webSearchTool({ name: 'web_search', type: 'web_search_20250305' })]\n\nconst processor = new StreamProcessor()\nfor await (const chunk of chat({\n  adapter,\n  tools,\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Find two sources on the drone market.' }],\n})) {\n  processor.processChunk(chunk)\n}\nprocessor.finalizeStream()\n\n// The follow-up turn can still cite the previous search results.\nconst followUp = chat({\n  adapter,\n  tools,\n  messages: [\n    ...processor.getMessages(),\n    { role: 'user', content: 'List the exact sources you used.' },\n  ],\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The search/fetch call surfaces as a provider-executed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tool-call"},{"type":"text","value":" part on the\nassistant message; the agent loop never tries to run it client-side."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"applyPatchTool"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"localShellTool"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"shellTool({ environment: { type: \"local\" } })"},{"type":"text","value":" are different. The model returns the call, and your app runs it. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/openai.md#applypatchtool","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"read-web-search-sources","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read web search sources"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI and Gemini web search calls expose a common "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata.sources"},{"type":"text","value":" array on\nthe assistant tool-call part. Each source has a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"url"},{"type":"text","value":" and can also include a\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"title"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pageAge"},{"type":"text","value":". Use this list to render source links in your UI. The\nprovider still owns search execution, so do not execute the tool call in your\napplication."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { getProviderExecutedMetadata } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport type { UIMessage } from '@tanstack/ai'\n\nfunction logSources(message: UIMessage) {\n  for (const part of message.parts) {\n    if (part.type !== 'tool-call') continue\n    const sources = getProviderExecutedMetadata(part)?.sources ?? []\n    for (const source of sources) {\n      console.log(source.title ?? source.url, source.url)\n    }\n  }\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The raw provider response stays available for provider-specific handling under\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata.openai"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata.gemini"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-level-guard","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type-level guard"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every provider-specific tool factory (e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"webSearchTool"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"computerUseTool"},{"type":"text","value":")\nreturns a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ProviderTool<TProvider, TKind>"},{"type":"text","value":" brand. The adapter's\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolCapabilities"},{"type":"text","value":" (derived from each model's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"supports.tools"},{"type":"text","value":" list) gates\nwhich brands are assignable to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tools"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Paste a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"computerUseTool(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" into a model that doesn't expose it, and\nTypeScript reports an error on that array element — not on the factory call,\nnot at runtime. User-defined "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolDefinition()"},{"type":"text","value":" tools stay unbranded and\nalways assignable. The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"customTool"},{"type":"text","value":" factories exported from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ai-anthropic"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ai-openai"},{"type":"text","value":" also return a plain "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Tool"},{"type":"text","value":" (not a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ProviderTool"},{"type":"text","value":" brand) and are\ntherefore universally accepted by any chat model, just like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolDefinition()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"available-tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Available tools"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tools"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Anthropic"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"webSearchTool"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"webFetchTool"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"codeExecutionTool"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"computerUseTool"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"bashTool"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"textEditorTool"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"memoryTool"},{"type":"text","value":" — see "},{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/anthropic.md#provider-tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Anthropic adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"webSearchTool"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"webSearchPreviewTool"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fileSearchTool"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"imageGenerationTool"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"codeInterpreterTool"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mcpTool"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"computerUseTool"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"localShellTool"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"shellTool"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"applyPatchTool"},{"type":"text","value":" — see "},{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/openai.md#provider-tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Gemini"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"codeExecutionTool"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fileSearchTool"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"googleSearchTool"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"googleSearchRetrievalTool"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"googleMapsTool"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"urlContextTool"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"computerUseTool"},{"type":"text","value":" — see "},{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/gemini.md#provider-tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Gemini adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenRouter"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"webSearchTool"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"webFetchTool"},{"type":"text","value":" — see "},{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/openrouter.md#provider-tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenRouter adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grok"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"function tools only (no provider-specific tools)."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Groq"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"function tools only (no provider-specific tools)."}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"which-models-support-which-tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Which models support which tools?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each adapter's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"supports.tools"},{"type":"text","value":" array is the source of truth. The comparison\nmatrix is maintained alongside "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"model-meta.ts"},{"type":"text","value":" and reflected here:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Anthropic"}]},{"type":"text","value":": every registered model supports the full tool superset,\nexcept four. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"claude-opus-5-5"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"claude-sonnet-5-5"},{"type":"text","value":", and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"claude-haiku-5-5"},{"type":"text","value":" support every tool but "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"computerUseTool"},{"type":"text","value":", and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"claude-opus-5-fast"},{"type":"text","value":" supports none. The\nretired Claude 3.x models with narrower support were removed."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI"}]},{"type":"text","value":": GPT-5 family and reasoning models (O-series) support the full\nsuperset. GPT-6 Astra, Sol, and Luna support every tool except\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"webSearchPreviewTool"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"localShellTool"},{"type":"text","value":". GPT-4-series supports\nweb/file/image/code/mcp but not preview/shell variants. GPT-3.5 and\naudio-focused models: none."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Gemini"}]},{"type":"text","value":": 3.x Pro/Flash models support the full tool set. Lite and\nimage/video variants have narrower support."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenRouter"}]},{"type":"text","value":": every chat model supports "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"webSearchTool"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"webFetchTool"},{"type":"text","value":" via the gateway."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For the exact per-model list, open the adapter page or read the model's\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"supports.tools"},{"type":"text","value":" array directly from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"model-meta.ts"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"provider-skills","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider Skills"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Anthropic and OpenAI support hosted, provider-managed skill bundles that run\ninside the provider's server-side sandbox. Skills attach to an execution tool\n("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"codeExecutionTool"},{"type":"text","value":" for Anthropic, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"shellTool"},{"type":"text","value":" for OpenAI) and are referenced\nby ID — the provider handles installation and execution."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"./provider-skills.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider Skills"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for full setup steps and examples."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"migrating-from-earlier-versions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Migrating from earlier versions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you were using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createWebSearchTool"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-openrouter"},{"type":"text","value":", see\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../migration/migration.md#6-provider-tools-moved-to-tools-subpath","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Migration Guide §6"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"import","text":"Import","level":2},{"id":"use-in-chat-tools","text":"Use in chat({ tools })","level":2},{"id":"multi-turn-persistence","text":"Multi-turn persistence","level":2},{"id":"read-web-search-sources","text":"Read web search sources","level":3},{"id":"type-level-guard","text":"Type-level guard","level":2},{"id":"available-tools","text":"Available tools","level":2},{"id":"which-models-support-which-tools","text":"Which models support which tools?","level":2},{"id":"provider-skills","text":"Provider Skills","level":2},{"id":"migrating-from-earlier-versions","text":"Migrating from earlier versions","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nMost providers expose native tools beyond user-defined function calls: web\nsearch, code execution, computer use, hosted retrieval, and more. TanStack AI\nexports each provider's native tools from a dedicated `/tools` subpath per\nadapter package.\n\nYou have an adapter already wired up. You want to give the model access to a\nprovider-native capability (e.g. Anthropic web search) and be sure you never\npair a tool with a model that doesn't support it. By the end of this page,\nyou'll have imported the factory, added it to `chat({ tools: [...] })`, and\nunderstood the compile-time guard that will catch unsupported combinations.\n\n## Import\n\nEvery adapter ships provider tools on a `/tools` subpath:\n\n```typescript\nimport { webSearchTool } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic/tools'\nimport { codeInterpreterTool } from '@tanstack/ai-openai/tools'\nimport { googleSearchTool } from '@tanstack/ai-gemini/tools'\n```\n\n## Use in `chat({ tools })`\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { anthropicText } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\nimport { webSearchTool } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic/tools'\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: anthropicText('claude-opus-4-6'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: \"Summarize today's AI news.\" }],\n  tools: [\n    webSearchTool({\n      name: 'web_search',\n      type: 'web_search_20250305',\n      max_uses: 3,\n    }),\n  ],\n})\n```\n\nThe factory is what selects native provider behavior, not the public name. A plain function named `web_search`, `google_search`, or `code_execution` stays a custom function. Do not hand-build `{ name: 'web_search', metadata: ... }` and expect a native payload.\n\nYou can put a factory tool and your own function in the same `chat({ tools })` call if the names differ. Tool names in one `tools` array must be unique. If you pass both `webSearchTool()` and your own function named `web_search`, `chat()` throws `DuplicateToolNameError` before it talks to the provider.\n\n## Multi-turn persistence\n\nProvider tools run on the provider's own infrastructure, so their results\n(e.g. Anthropic `web_search` sources, `web_fetch` page contents) come back\nembedded in the assistant turn rather than as a separate tool message. TanStack\nAI preserves those results on the assistant message, so when you feed the prior\nconversation back into the next `chat()` call the model still sees the earlier\nevidence — no special handling required:\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, StreamProcessor } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { anthropicText } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\nimport { webSearchTool } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic/tools'\n\nconst adapter = anthropicText('claude-opus-4-6')\nconst tools = [webSearchTool({ name: 'web_search', type: 'web_search_20250305' })]\n\nconst processor = new StreamProcessor()\nfor await (const chunk of chat({\n  adapter,\n  tools,\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Find two sources on the drone market.' }],\n})) {\n  processor.processChunk(chunk)\n}\nprocessor.finalizeStream()\n\n// The follow-up turn can still cite the previous search results.\nconst followUp = chat({\n  adapter,\n  tools,\n  messages: [\n    ...processor.getMessages(),\n    { role: 'user', content: 'List the exact sources you used.' },\n  ],\n})\n```\n\nThe search/fetch call surfaces as a provider-executed `tool-call` part on the\nassistant message; the agent loop never tries to run it client-side.\n\nOpenAI `applyPatchTool`, `localShellTool`, and `shellTool({ environment: { type: \"local\" } })` are different. The model returns the call, and your app runs it. See [OpenAI adapter](../adapters/openai.md#applypatchtool).\n\n### Read web search sources\n\nOpenAI and Gemini web search calls expose a common `metadata.sources` array on\nthe assistant tool-call part. Each source has a `url` and can also include a\n`title` or `pageAge`. Use this list to render source links in your UI. The\nprovider still owns search execution, so do not execute the tool call in your\napplication.\n\n```typescript\nimport { getProviderExecutedMetadata } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport type { UIMessage } from '@tanstack/ai'\n\nfunction logSources(message: UIMessage) {\n  for (const part of message.parts) {\n    if (part.type !== 'tool-call') continue\n    const sources = getProviderExecutedMetadata(part)?.sources ?? []\n    for (const source of sources) {\n      console.log(source.title ?? source.url, source.url)\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe raw provider response stays available for provider-specific handling under\n`metadata.openai` or `metadata.gemini`.\n\n## Type-level guard\n\nEvery provider-specific tool factory (e.g. `webSearchTool`, `computerUseTool`)\nreturns a `ProviderTool<TProvider, TKind>` brand. The adapter's\n`toolCapabilities` (derived from each model's `supports.tools` list) gates\nwhich brands are assignable to `tools`.\n\nPaste a `computerUseTool(...)` into a model that doesn't expose it, and\nTypeScript reports an error on that array element — not on the factory call,\nnot at runtime. User-defined `toolDefinition()` tools stay unbranded and\nalways assignable. The `customTool` factories exported from `ai-anthropic` and\n`ai-openai` also return a plain `Tool` (not a `ProviderTool` brand) and are\ntherefore universally accepted by any chat model, just like `toolDefinition()`.\n\n## Available tools\n\n| Provider | Tools |\n|---|---|\n| Anthropic | `webSearchTool`, `webFetchTool`, `codeExecutionTool`, `computerUseTool`, `bashTool`, `textEditorTool`, `memoryTool` — see [Anthropic adapter](../adapters/anthropic.md#provider-tools). |\n| OpenAI | `webSearchTool`, `webSearchPreviewTool`, `fileSearchTool`, `imageGenerationTool`, `codeInterpreterTool`, `mcpTool`, `computerUseTool`, `localShellTool`, `shellTool`, `applyPatchTool` — see [OpenAI adapter](../adapters/openai.md#provider-tools). |\n| Gemini | `codeExecutionTool`, `fileSearchTool`, `googleSearchTool`, `googleSearchRetrievalTool`, `googleMapsTool`, `urlContextTool`, `computerUseTool` — see [Gemini adapter](../adapters/gemini.md#provider-tools). |\n| OpenRouter | `webSearchTool`, `webFetchTool` — see [OpenRouter adapter](../adapters/openrouter.md#provider-tools). |\n| Grok | function tools only (no provider-specific tools). |\n| Groq | function tools only (no provider-specific tools). |\n\n## Which models support which tools?\n\nEach adapter's `supports.tools` array is the source of truth. The comparison\nmatrix is maintained alongside `model-meta.ts` and reflected here:\n\n- **Anthropic**: every registered model supports the full tool superset,\n  except four. `claude-opus-5-5`, `claude-sonnet-5-5`, and\n  `claude-haiku-5-5` support every tool but `computerUseTool`, and\n  `claude-opus-5-fast` supports none. The\n  retired Claude 3.x models with narrower support were removed.\n- **OpenAI**: GPT-5 family and reasoning models (O-series) support the full\n  superset. GPT-6 Astra, Sol, and Luna support every tool except\n  `webSearchPreviewTool` and `localShellTool`. GPT-4-series supports\n  web/file/image/code/mcp but not preview/shell variants. GPT-3.5 and\n  audio-focused models: none.\n- **Gemini**: 3.x Pro/Flash models support the full tool set. Lite and\n  image/video variants have narrower support.\n- **OpenRouter**: every chat model supports `webSearchTool` and\n  `webFetchTool` via the gateway.\n\nFor the exact per-model list, open the adapter page or read the model's\n`supports.tools` array directly from `model-meta.ts`.\n\n## Provider Skills\n\nAnthropic and OpenAI support hosted, provider-managed skill bundles that run\ninside the provider's server-side sandbox. Skills attach to an execution tool\n(`codeExecutionTool` for Anthropic, `shellTool` for OpenAI) and are referenced\nby ID — the provider handles installation and execution.\n\nSee [Provider Skills](./provider-skills.md) for full setup steps and examples.\n\n## Migrating from earlier versions\n\nIf you were using `createWebSearchTool` from `@tanstack/ai-openrouter`, see\n[Migration Guide §6](../migration/migration.md#6-provider-tools-moved-to-tools-subpath).\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Provider Tools\nid: provider-tools\norder: 2\n---\n\nMost providers expose native tools beyond user-defined function calls: web\nsearch, code execution, computer use, hosted retrieval, and more. TanStack AI\nexports each provider's native tools from a dedicated `/tools` subpath per\nadapter package.\n\nYou have an adapter already wired up. You want to give the model access to a\nprovider-native capability (e.g. Anthropic web search) and be sure you never\npair a tool with a model that doesn't support it. By the end of this page,\nyou'll have imported the factory, added it to `chat({ tools: [...] })`, and\nunderstood the compile-time guard that will catch unsupported combinations.\n\n## Import\n\nEvery adapter ships provider tools on a `/tools` subpath:\n\n```typescript\nimport { webSearchTool } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic/tools'\nimport { codeInterpreterTool } from '@tanstack/ai-openai/tools'\nimport { googleSearchTool } from '@tanstack/ai-gemini/tools'\n```\n\n## Use in `chat({ tools })`\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { anthropicText } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\nimport { webSearchTool } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic/tools'\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: anthropicText('claude-opus-4-6'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: \"Summarize today's AI news.\" }],\n  tools: [\n    webSearchTool({\n      name: 'web_search',\n      type: 'web_search_20250305',\n      max_uses: 3,\n    }),\n  ],\n})\n```\n\nThe factory is what selects native provider behavior, not the public name. A plain function named `web_search`, `google_search`, or `code_execution` stays a custom function. Do not hand-build `{ name: 'web_search', metadata: ... }` and expect a native payload.\n\nYou can put a factory tool and your own function in the same `chat({ tools })` call if the names differ. Tool names in one `tools` array must be unique. If you pass both `webSearchTool()` and your own function named `web_search`, `chat()` throws `DuplicateToolNameError` before it talks to the provider.\n\n## Multi-turn persistence\n\nProvider tools run on the provider's own infrastructure, so their results\n(e.g. Anthropic `web_search` sources, `web_fetch` page contents) come back\nembedded in the assistant turn rather than as a separate tool message. TanStack\nAI preserves those results on the assistant message, so when you feed the prior\nconversation back into the next `chat()` call the model still sees the earlier\nevidence — no special handling required:\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, StreamProcessor } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { anthropicText } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\nimport { webSearchTool } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic/tools'\n\nconst adapter = anthropicText('claude-opus-4-6')\nconst tools = [webSearchTool({ name: 'web_search', type: 'web_search_20250305' })]\n\nconst processor = new StreamProcessor()\nfor await (const chunk of chat({\n  adapter,\n  tools,\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Find two sources on the drone market.' }],\n})) {\n  processor.processChunk(chunk)\n}\nprocessor.finalizeStream()\n\n// The follow-up turn can still cite the previous search results.\nconst followUp = chat({\n  adapter,\n  tools,\n  messages: [\n    ...processor.getMessages(),\n    { role: 'user', content: 'List the exact sources you used.' },\n  ],\n})\n```\n\nThe search/fetch call surfaces as a provider-executed `tool-call` part on the\nassistant message; the agent loop never tries to run it client-side.\n\nOpenAI `applyPatchTool`, `localShellTool`, and `shellTool({ environment: { type: \"local\" } })` are different. The model returns the call, and your app runs it. See [OpenAI adapter](../adapters/openai.md#applypatchtool).\n\n### Read web search sources\n\nOpenAI and Gemini web search calls expose a common `metadata.sources` array on\nthe assistant tool-call part. Each source has a `url` and can also include a\n`title` or `pageAge`. Use this list to render source links in your UI. The\nprovider still owns search execution, so do not execute the tool call in your\napplication.\n\n```typescript\nimport { getProviderExecutedMetadata } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport type { UIMessage } from '@tanstack/ai'\n\nfunction logSources(message: UIMessage) {\n  for (const part of message.parts) {\n    if (part.type !== 'tool-call') continue\n    const sources = getProviderExecutedMetadata(part)?.sources ?? []\n    for (const source of sources) {\n      console.log(source.title ?? source.url, source.url)\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe raw provider response stays available for provider-specific handling under\n`metadata.openai` or `metadata.gemini`.\n\n## Type-level guard\n\nEvery provider-specific tool factory (e.g. `webSearchTool`, `computerUseTool`)\nreturns a `ProviderTool<TProvider, TKind>` brand. The adapter's\n`toolCapabilities` (derived from each model's `supports.tools` list) gates\nwhich brands are assignable to `tools`.\n\nPaste a `computerUseTool(...)` into a model that doesn't expose it, and\nTypeScript reports an error on that array element — not on the factory call,\nnot at runtime. User-defined `toolDefinition()` tools stay unbranded and\nalways assignable. The `customTool` factories exported from `ai-anthropic` and\n`ai-openai` also return a plain `Tool` (not a `ProviderTool` brand) and are\ntherefore universally accepted by any chat model, just like `toolDefinition()`.\n\n## Available tools\n\n| Provider | Tools |\n|---|---|\n| Anthropic | `webSearchTool`, `webFetchTool`, `codeExecutionTool`, `computerUseTool`, `bashTool`, `textEditorTool`, `memoryTool` — see [Anthropic adapter](../adapters/anthropic.md#provider-tools). |\n| OpenAI | `webSearchTool`, `webSearchPreviewTool`, `fileSearchTool`, `imageGenerationTool`, `codeInterpreterTool`, `mcpTool`, `computerUseTool`, `localShellTool`, `shellTool`, `applyPatchTool` — see [OpenAI adapter](../adapters/openai.md#provider-tools). |\n| Gemini | `codeExecutionTool`, `fileSearchTool`, `googleSearchTool`, `googleSearchRetrievalTool`, `googleMapsTool`, `urlContextTool`, `computerUseTool` — see [Gemini adapter](../adapters/gemini.md#provider-tools). |\n| OpenRouter | `webSearchTool`, `webFetchTool` — see [OpenRouter adapter](../adapters/openrouter.md#provider-tools). |\n| Grok | function tools only (no provider-specific tools). |\n| Groq | function tools only (no provider-specific tools). |\n\n## Which models support which tools?\n\nEach adapter's `supports.tools` array is the source of truth. The comparison\nmatrix is maintained alongside `model-meta.ts` and reflected here:\n\n- **Anthropic**: every registered model supports the full tool superset,\n  except four. `claude-opus-5-5`, `claude-sonnet-5-5`, and\n  `claude-haiku-5-5` support every tool but `computerUseTool`, and\n  `claude-opus-5-fast` supports none. The\n  retired Claude 3.x models with narrower support were removed.\n- **OpenAI**: GPT-5 family and reasoning models (O-series) support the full\n  superset. GPT-6 Astra, Sol, and Luna support every tool except\n  `webSearchPreviewTool` and `localShellTool`. GPT-4-series supports\n  web/file/image/code/mcp but not preview/shell variants. GPT-3.5 and\n  audio-focused models: none.\n- **Gemini**: 3.x Pro/Flash models support the full tool set. Lite and\n  image/video variants have narrower support.\n- **OpenRouter**: every chat model supports `webSearchTool` and\n  `webFetchTool` via the gateway.\n\nFor the exact per-model list, open the adapter page or read the model's\n`supports.tools` array directly from `model-meta.ts`.\n\n## Provider Skills\n\nAnthropic and OpenAI support hosted, provider-managed skill bundles that run\ninside the provider's server-side sandbox. Skills attach to an execution tool\n(`codeExecutionTool` for Anthropic, `shellTool` for OpenAI) and are referenced\nby ID — the provider handles installation and execution.\n\nSee [Provider Skills](./provider-skills.md) for full setup steps and examples.\n\n## Migrating from earlier versions\n\nIf you were using `createWebSearchTool` from `@tanstack/ai-openrouter`, see\n[Migration Guide §6](../migration/migration.md#6-provider-tools-moved-to-tools-subpath).\n"}
